    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "step_title": "Back of Bookshelf",
            "images": [
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/1yHbDWqJ26RSRyQa.medium",
                    "alt_text": "Back of Bookshelf Replacement, Back of Bookshelf: step 1, image 1 of 1"
                }
            ],
            "text": "Gather all pieces of the bookshelf if it fell apart or the shelf itself is still together.\nYou will need two people to complete this project.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/121749/234299"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/T4Wr1h4pGpRWuYVv.medium",
                    "alt_text": "Back of Bookshelf Replacement: step 2, image 1 of 3"
                },
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/fCfhtaLe5LcYaAhG.200x150",
                    "alt_text": "Back of Bookshelf Replacement: step 2, image 2 of 3"
                },
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HBum5wObJZRnnEoW.200x150",
                    "alt_text": "Back of Bookshelf Replacement: step 2, image 3 of 3"
                }
            ],
            "text": "You will need to put the bookshelf back together by holding the sides together.\nDrill new holes to insert new screws to reinforce the shelf. Use a 1/8 inch drill bit.\nPut screws into the freshly made holes with 1/8 by 1 inch wood screws to bring it together.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/121749/234301"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Now that the base of the bookshelf is back together, we will need to measure out the size of board needed for the new backing.\nUse the measuring tape and the square ruler to measure out the specific size you need. Use a pencil to draw the lines out so you can saw the piece out with precision.\nUse the jig saw to cut the piece of plywood out following the lines you just drew.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/121749/234302"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Line your new piece of plywood that you just cut, up with the back of the bookshelf.\nMake sure that the corners are lined up so that as you hammer in the nails it stays lined up and even.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/121749/234304"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Start from the top and work your way down each side when putting the nails in so the board doesn't bow.\nUse 2d penny nails and hammer them in along all four sides.\nFive nails on each of the four sides is all you will need.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/121749/234306"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "The shelf has its new plywood backing, so you can stand it up and you will feel the immediate difference in the sturdiness of your new shelf.\nPlace the shelf in the room of your choosing and place your books on it, knowing that it will not fall apart.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/121749/234308"
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "Finish Line",
